  partName: Intake Runner Left
  description: The Intake Runner Left is a medium-sized, compact component located
    at the middle-left-front of the engine, responsible for directing air-fuel mixture
    into the cylinders. Its accent-yellow material provides visual distinction and
    helps to identify the component during maintenance, and its position enables
    efficient airflow into the engine. Interestingly, the Intake Runner Left is designed
    to work in conjunction with its right counterpart to ensure balanced airflow
    and optimal engine performance.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
